# Herd local development

Laravel Herd (Pro) on Windows is the only supported local set-up. This repository is its own Herd site at <https://myapes-account.test>: nginx with PHP 8.4 (pinned with `herd isolate`) through FastCGI, Herd's MySQL 8.4 service (`myapes_account_local`), Herd's mail catcher on SMTP 2525, Node 22 from Herd's nvm and Vite on port 5175, with the values in `docs/herd/profile.md` (`docs/herd/profile.json` for the scripts). Never suggest containers, virtual machines or any other local stack for local development.

## Before any development work: the live preview gate

Cursor's `live-preview-gate` and `herd-local-preview` skills own the gate. This repository fills its slots:

| Slot | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Preview command | `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\preview.ps1` (exit 3 = a decision to ask about, exit 1 = a blocker to report) |
| Preview URL | <https://myapes-account.test> (Herd site `myapes-account`) |
| HMR | Vite at `https://myapes-account.test:5175`, started by the script with no window, output in `storage/logs/vite-dev.log`; stop with `scripts\preview.ps1 -StopDevServer` |
| Health check | `/healthz` shows the checked-out revision, PHP 8.4 and `php_sapi` `cgi-fcgi` in its `local` block |

The script stops on uncommitted tracked files, fetches, fast-forwards, merges `origin/main` (never a rebase), runs `composer install` or `npm ci` when a lock file changed, reports pending migrations (ask before running them), checks Herd and its MySQL are running and that `/healthz` matches, then starts or reuses this repository's Vite. Never start Vite or `npm run dev` in a window of its own, and use host names, not IP addresses, for the preview.

## Herd

- Command line: dot-source `scripts\herd-env.ps1` to put Herd's PHP 8.4, Composer, MySQL client and Node 22 first on `PATH` (Herd's global defaults may be PHP 8.5 and another Node), or use `herd php` and `herd composer`.
- Set up or repair with `composer setup` (`scripts/herd-setup.ps1`). Demo data: `composer demo:seed` and `composer demo:reset`, which refuse unless `APP_ENV=local`.
- Debug with the Herd MCP tools (`site` `error`, `logs`, `insights`, `mail`), passing `site: "myapes-account"`.
- PHP settings in `public/.htaccess` stay inside `<IfModule php_module>` (Cloudron runs PHP as an Apache module); their local equivalents are in `public/.user.ini`, which Herd's PHP reads. Keep the `HTTP_AUTHORIZATION` rewrite rule.
- Herd's settings (PHP versions, services, SSL, restarts) belong to Bambie: ask with AskQuestion before changing them, and never touch other sites, their databases or links.
